<!DOCTYPE html>
(# One problem as a page a browser can open, from `file://` with the network off.

   There is no script here and no stylesheet link, which is the point: the maths was typeset
   into SVG by `core/html/mathjax.py` at build time and the CSS is inlined, so the page needs
   nothing but itself and the `pictures/` directory beside it. Firefox gives every `file://`
   document its own origin, so anything it had to fetch -- even from a sibling directory -- it
   would not get. #)
<html lang="(* lang *)">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>(* title *)</title>
<style>(* css *)</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
    <h1>(* title *)</h1>
    (* content *)
</main>
</body>
</html>
